From 709956ca8e953e6f911081e5a07594223532912b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Knifethrower <andersenpeters@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:07:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 32/34] render: keep the shared atlas's run-time rows in a
 texture of their own

The shared atlas (4096x5120 RGBA, 80 MiB on the default resources) mixed
what is packed once with what the game writes while it runs: font glyphs,
the map, skin, trim and icon slots, the on-screen keyboard's text and the
animated sprites. An ASTC texture only takes whole-block writes, so none of
it could be compressed (the bake beside the spill went unused).

Pack the two apart: everything written at run time below everything packed
once, from an ASTC block row (HudAtlas::static_rows), the glyph rows last.
Shelves packed apart took 6144 rows for what fitted 5120 mixed, so the
layout is now a bottom-left skyline, which packs both parts in 5120 again:
2152 static rows and 2968 below them on the default resources.

On the GPU each part is a texture of its own (gfx/shared_atlas.rs), and
run-time writes go to the part they fall in. Atlas coordinates keep their
meaning: hud.wgsl, entity.wgsl, screen.wgsl and oit_clouds.wgsl read the two
as one atlas as tall as both (atlas_sample, atlas_load, atlas_size), which
needs no new uniform, only the two textures' sizes.

What samples the atlas without those shaders gets SharedAtlas::combined, the
whole atlas in one texture, made the first time it is asked for and kept
up to date from then on: a resource pack's text shader, a shader pack (its
celestial sampler and weather copies), and a native mod that sets
RenderNeeds::atlas (new; WorldDrawn::atlas is None otherwise).

No memory changes yet: the next patch loads the static part from its ASTC
bake. In a still scene (frozen ticks: mobs, a held filled map, animated
hotbar items, a chat line of characters the bitmap fonts lack) frames match
the previous build's except where two runs of the same build differ too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
